goal oriented psuedo code 

The goal is to determine the ranking of neighbors for a given prefix and observer. 
the best path to a given prefix is given in the observer's FIB. 
Fibs are built from a set of updates where each update contains the prefix P, the AS PATH to p (A), and a timestamp T. Let an update be denoted as U(P,A,T)
Let the best path for P be denoted as F(P,A,T)
FIBS are built from a set of updates over a timerange, T-i to time T, where the best path over this sequence is selected and accepted into the FIB. 

It must be the case that in order for an observer to hear an update U, it must be sent by some neighbor N. In fact, this neighbor is the last (0th index) [technically the 1st index because we get it from the RIB, but semantics], AS in the AS Path of the Update, from the observer's persepctive. 

BGP Routers perform BGP Best Path Selection in order to determine the router's best path to P. The selection criteria follows as an ordered list, where if a result is found based on the selection criteria, the route is immidiately accepted without performing later steps of the route selection. <For purposes of this discussion, we will focus on the first 4 methods:>

highest weight (cisco) 
highest local preference 
prefer locally originated 
AS PATH 
Lowest Origin type, prefers IGP over EGP over Incomplete 
lowest MED 
eBGP over iBGP 
lowest IGP metric to next BGP hop 
prefer older routes (sort of, time gets removed from RIB entry)
lower router ID (router's ip address) 
Lower neighbor address (routers ip address) 

let U1 U2 be defined as U1(P,A1,T1) and U2(P,A2,T2)
When will U1 be selected over U2? 
Let |U1| and |U2| denote the AS Path Length of field A1 and A2 respectively. The first criteria of path selection we can reason about is AS Path, so if 
|U1| > |U2| but U1 is in the FIB, then clearly it was accepted by some metric before AS PATH length. 
if |U1| = |U2| then it was accepted by some method that is not AS Path 
if |U1| < |U2| then it was likely accepted by AS PATH, or some field before. At the very most AS Path is the ultimate reason. However, we cannot claim that AS Path is the reason, since we do not know for certain that it is the reason. 
> BEFORE AS Path 
= NOT AS PATH 
< AS PATH or Before 

